  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- Fixed: In previous version, using `System.Runtime.CompilerServices.RuntimeHelpers.GetUninitializedObject` caused `IL2072` trimming warnings.\n        We now changed handling of completions so that we never need an uninitialized instance of definition type, thus removed usage of `GetUninitializedObject`\n        to fix the issue:\n        - `ICliAddCompletions` interface is now renamed to `ICliGetCompletions`.\n        - `void AddCompletions(string propertyName, List<Func<CompletionContext, IEnumerable<CompletionItem>>> completionSources)` interface method\n          is now changed to `Enumerable<CompletionItem> GetCompletions(string propertyName, CompletionContext completionContext)`.\n        So now, instead we will use `Bind` method to get cached definition instance and call `GetCompletions` interface method.\n        The signature change also made implementing interface method more easy and straightforward.",
  "repository": "",
  "verbatimVersion": "2.4.3",
